[{"id":"VRCE-2-72-1","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":72,"verse":1,"english":"Then ſatrughna, the younger brother of Lakşmaņa spoke to Bharata burning in grief as he was revolving in his mind the (intended) journey (to Rāma).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.803,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-78-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2072001","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6dd2d572f1bbe42432db1a83ec221f2ad164667fdae8628dda8f606e6ea3d91f","compact":"b3f9b47206a8d3666e90e9d278ff186f31e8c7faedfec0e8105af1b119afbf0c","nasal":"9751c536882a630567330deaad8b210e844bf5717b56bd1a7587b888de0956eb"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-72-2","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":72,"verse":2,"english":"Need it be said that Rāma is the refuge both of himself and all creatures in trouble? That Rāma possessed of strength has been exiled into the woods by a woman!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.886,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-78-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2072002","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8e020d26f4659c44d01400912e371f6b14ba72a0cdb08987978b7a36149c9bdb","compact":"8aa742ffd6d89f5817a593a3b9dd9120d85adf62f1dda537af497bc3fbb81b64","nasal":"edde6decba5ac0288b623492c3874ac1efdbc6215811ce3bb81356d719dfea56"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-72-3","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":72,"verse":3,"english":"And powerful and having prowess, why did not Laksmana deliver Rāma by checking our father?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-78-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2072003","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9605257dd9f3b37f8f8e2f5d4a0583244a36105013a41ee2c9ba4ffa980c1292","compact":"c9d88ed140d449770cd0cf2cceca800cbe493c37849fd303200bf3ea0dc50c93","nasal":"8fd2028318db7e20b75e51507c49d65088573fd7248a1d6e43a1ac8c379872ee"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-72-4","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":72,"verse":4,"english":"The king bent upon following an unrighteous course through the influence of a woman, should, the justice or otherwise of the measure being fully weighed, at the very outset have been checked.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-78-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2072004","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4e432e3cb9e794e6efdb8273b20d5e9b106f8335468cfd0b1ea398ecd3ff08e6","compact":"1664fd07cae4969a484429b1505a9dee837e2c36163949ae34ca7e9ba6b34d7f","nasal":"1664fd07cae4969a484429b1505a9dee837e2c36163949ae34ca7e9ba6b34d7f"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-72-5","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":72,"verse":5,"english":"As Lakşmaņa's younger brother Satrughna was speaking thus, appeared there at the door in front the hump backed one adorned with every kind of ornament, with her body besmeared with sandal paste, wearing regal apparel, and variously decked out with a variety of ornaments.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.791,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-78-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2072005","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1432784120a74af87739dcecbfe69b544e7a900139268a96781af191bed51390","compact":"6d7ad22ded3a4c35cede7a53a0aafdd376eef929b0e4b223135b5e8d8662ee88","nasal":"6d7ad22ded3a4c35cede7a53a0aafdd376eef929b0e4b223135b5e8d8662ee88"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-72-6","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":72,"verse":6,"english":"As Lakşmaņa's younger brother Satrughna was speaking thus, appeared there at the door in front the hump backed one adorned with every kind of ornament, with her body besmeared with sandal paste, wearing regal apparel, and variously decked out with a variety of ornaments.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.452,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-78-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2072006","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b6c18403ac6c189cc2795fd88af1119b9e58c78b13500949e319d0fc24d82663","compact":"6946b1755f31ca2f4070bbb9dc65ec400650f1462032aa706cca5360f07e802f","nasal":"74de5bf8f07741d9fc5c41919e37f77faf34944f133a9e5cfac14f89fd834913"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-72-7","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":72,"verse":7,"english":"At that time seeing that one of horrible misdeeds, (Bharata) who stood near the door, seizing the hump backed one ruthlessly, took her to Satrughna, and said.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.89,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-78-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2072007","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"88a3f9d6d688f44ec301a034a918662637145a4f277bb1461ee1957f2504dc69","compact":"e5e8fd415e09383f7803ae015e9509dc497133a50e6fd2b3947bf89951bfbbfd","nasal":"e5e8fd415e09383f7803ae015e9509dc497133a50e6fd2b3947bf89951bfbbfd"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-72-8","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":72,"verse":8,"english":"That one through whom Rāma has gone to the wood and our father has renounced his body this is that wicked and remorseless one. Do you deal with her as you like.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-78-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2072008","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b5e69f917ccb6b71019654626ef203c2b94cd2c1098d3c57318660b62339925d","compact":"4c349fb939e120a61310c5a23addc944bcd2d6f90faf2ccdca45c24114b55869","nasal":"4c349fb939e120a61310c5a23addc944bcd2d6f90faf2ccdca45c24114b55869"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-72-9","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":72,"verse":9,"english":"At Bharata's command Satrughna observing vows waxing exceedingly aggrieved, addressed all the inmates of the inner apartment, saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-78-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2072009","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"63d7c7c1066ee5bcc1ed03212c5dce211639a03fd6b84754f1d832c9a1a41511","compact":"e176fc991a8ae8bd21927b1492d3aaa2e46845d3aa302dc44ffea2c5bcd39e8d","nasal":"0091ca6f7d1abd1e79d2151249ea6975626879be39294b092395f65462ded6d8"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-72-10","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":72,"verse":10,"english":"This one has occasioned intense misery to my father and brothers Let her now take the fruit of her fell deed.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.75,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-78-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2072010","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"41b5dab32eea2990fc4dba841980c1fbab1148a3e58864adacf5fb876b5c7880","compact":"f5374460688ed199d185ced1127782181b5b4241dbd24004d704adf82f38f7c4","nasal":"f5374460688ed199d185ced1127782181b5b4241dbd24004d704adf82f38f7c4"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-72-11","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":72,"verse":11,"english":"Having said this, he furiously fell upon the hump backed one surrounded by her maids. Thereupon she with her cries made the chamber resound.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.865,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-78-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2072011","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4f83874b5f96953d7d081e79569de1c254be9c08c42e84fb594629f721fe12b9","compact":"ca8f6198924887243c7baf5f633a5df22c12d57c13c8603fe601eef4f624c210","nasal":"ca8f6198924887243c7baf5f633a5df22c12d57c13c8603fe601eef4f624c210"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-72-12","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":72,"verse":12,"english":"Concluding Śatrughna fired with rage, her associates extremely pained, fled away in all directions.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-78-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2072012","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e5cc89147043aa3e8c2e4e9bdecc01b3717d074e8057b66cad2d68612da6d910","compact":"3709503ce6bf11c1f0fced97369d475fec4ca92a75e5199de3ad83b3437c3b92","nasal":"3709503ce6bf11c1f0fced97369d475fec4ca92a75e5199de3ad83b3437c3b92"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-72-13","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":72,"verse":13,"english":"Then her companions in a body took counsel of each other, saying, “considering the way in which he has entered upon it, he will annihilate us quite.\"","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.758,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-78-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2072013","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a0252cfacbe3460c79ae76a2cea3eb9fa23d24e81a4a541b8aff6c3d6239eef7","compact":"6c0bd84aa66ddaf0e5f7bc793cced9b1703e86085393fdb783b15c18aff46ff4","nasal":"ecbf0d5ad70133e1c5b4ad1d030a78696c8921cd68f069a0e4ab1f43f427b7bd"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-72-14","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":72,"verse":14,"english":"Let us therefore seek the protection of the tender hearted generous, pious and illustrious Kausalyā. Even she is our sure refuge.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.884,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-78-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2072014","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a1a1c592031ac6b7